# start Validation Reply Form
_vrf_ATOM007_a                   
;
PROBLEM: _atom_site_aniso_label is missing
RESPONSE: Due to electron beam damage, Uiso are used in the refinement.
;
_vrf_RINTA01_a                   
;
PROBLEM: The value of Rint is greater than 0.25
RESPONSE: Electron diffraction data normally has high Rint values.
;
_vrf_THETM01_a                   
;
PROBLEM: The value of sine(theta_max)/wavelength is less than 0.550
RESPONSE: Because of the bad crystallization, the Signal to Noise ratio is not optimized, resulting in a low resolution.
;
_vrf_PLAT020_a                   
;
PROBLEM: The Value of Rint is Greater Than 0.12 .........      0.404 Report
RESPONSE: Electron diffraction data normally has high Rint values.
;
_vrf_PLAT026_a                   
;
PROBLEM: Ratio Observed / Unique Reflections (too) Low ..        18% Check
RESPONSE: The low ratio of observed / unique reflections is due to the low electron dose and short exposure time used for data collection in order to minimize the beam damage.
;
_vrf_PLAT082_a                   
;
PROBLEM: High R1 Value ..................................       0.32 Report
RESPONSE: Electron diffraction data normally has high R1 values.
;
_vrf_PLAT084_a                   
;
PROBLEM: High wR2 Value (i.e. > 0.25) ...................       0.71 Report
RESPONSE: Electron diffraction data normally has high wR2 values.
;
_vrf_PLAT340_a                   
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............    0.06479 Ang.
RESPONSE: Variations in C--C bond lengths arise from the applied geometric constraints (AFIX 66/DFIX) and the disordered nature of the crystal structure.
;
_vrf_PLAT602_a                   
;
PROBLEM: Solvent Accessible VOID(S) in the Unit-Cell ....          ! Check
RESPONSE: This is expected in this porous COF.
;
